  "tagline": "Distributed SQL query engine from Meta for interactive queries over data lakes and many sources.",
  "description": "Presto is the federated SQL query engine Facebook open-sourced in 2013 and now governed by the Presto Foundation under the Linux Foundation. It has no storage of its own: coordinators plan ANSI SQL and workers pull data through connectors for Hive, Iceberg, Delta, Hudi, Kafka, relational databases and more. The project's focus has shifted to Prestissimo, a C++ worker built on Meta's Velox library that replaces the Java workers for much better efficiency. Presto remains a solid lakehouse engine at Meta and Uber, though Trino (the 2019 fork) has the larger community today.",
